From: Spaceghost <Spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] install binaries owner-writable

Buildroot strips target binaries as the unprivileged build user after package
installation.  Installing dhcpcd mode 0555 prevents that finalizer from
rewriting the binary, leaving debug information in production images.  Mode
0755 retains the same runtime access while allowing the owner to strip it.

---
 Makefile.inc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.inc b/Makefile.inc
index ad7e43a..8ae0a8f 100644
--- a/Makefile.inc
+++ b/Makefile.inc
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 PICFLAG?=	-fPIC
 
-BINMODE?=	0555
+BINMODE?=	0755
 NONBINMODE?=	0444
 MANMODE?=	${NONBINMODE}
 CONFMODE?=	0644
-- 
2.39.5
